**Summary:** Wave-defense FPS in \`project/\` (Three.js r160, vendored locally — fully offline-capable). 64×64m courtyard arena, Sketchfab GLB enemy soldier with CPU calibration + procedural fallback, procedural rifle viewmodel (recoil/ADS/reload/muzzle-flash/tracers), bot AI waves with strafing/bursts, exploding barrels, resupply depot, HUD + minimap + killfeed + procedural WebAudio. Built with fanned-out subagents (weapon/map/AI/audio-VFX specs) and iterated under harsh screenshot critique (spawn facing, recoil model, enemy separation/facing, hit-flash bleed, flash sprite).

**Game:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/tree/opencode/34010515573/project — open \`project/index.html\` (or serve \`project/\` over HTTP; GLB + modules need http).
**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/$SHA
**Tests:** node syntax check OK; real headless-Chromium runs with **0 console/page errors**; verified state=play, bots spawn, GLB loads, kills score (450, headshots ×150), waves advance (wave 2 reached), reload/resupply work.
**Known limitations:** Visuals are stylized low-poly, not literal CoD parity (browser/procedural constraints); no multiplayer; pointer-lock play needs a real browser (headless verified via ?autostart demo mode).

